1
00:00:00,360 --> 00:00:03,580
A transversal cutting two parallel lines makes eight angles.

2
00:00:03,580 --> 00:00:06,384
Those eight angles are linked by six relationships, and

3
00:00:06,384 --> 00:00:10,251
those relationships turn a diagram into an equation.

4
00:00:10,917 --> 00:00:12,708
Two lines in the same plane that never meet

5
00:00:12,708 --> 00:00:16,410
are called parallel lines. Here they are, with the

6
00:00:16,410 --> 00:00:18,757
same arrow mark on each. A line that cuts

7
00:00:18,757 --> 00:00:22,522
across them is called a transversal. It crosses both

8
00:00:22,522 --> 00:00:25,417
parallel lines and makes eight angles, four at each

9
00:00:25,417 --> 00:00:29,068
crossing. The whole lesson lives in that one figure.

10
00:00:29,893 --> 00:00:32,557
At each crossing there are four angles, so the

11
00:00:32,557 --> 00:00:35,303
figure has eight angles in all. We number them

12
00:00:35,303 --> 00:00:39,233
from one to eight, going around each crossing. Angles

13
00:00:39,233 --> 00:00:42,453
three, four, five and six lie between the two

14
00:00:42,453 --> 00:00:47,053
parallel lines: these are the interior angles. Angles one,

15
00:00:47,053 --> 00:00:50,453
two, seven and eight lie outside the lines: these

16
00:00:50,453 --> 00:00:52,404
are the exterior angles.

17
00:00:52,947 --> 00:00:56,543
Start at the upper crossing. Angles one and four

18
00:00:56,543 --> 00:01:00,404
are vertically opposite, so they are equal. Angles one

19
00:01:00,404 --> 00:01:01,862
and two lie side by side on the straight

20
00:01:01,862 --> 00:01:03,824
line, so they form a linear pair and add

21
00:01:03,824 --> 00:01:06,778
up to one hundred and eighty degrees. The same

22
00:01:06,778 --> 00:01:08,458
is true at the lower crossing.

23
00:01:09,077 --> 00:01:12,287
Corresponding angles sit in the same position at the

24
00:01:12,287 --> 00:01:14,766
two crossings. Angle one and angle five are both

25
00:01:14,766 --> 00:01:18,817
at the top left, so they correspond, and they

26
00:01:18,817 --> 00:01:21,137
are equal. Angle two and angle six are both

27
00:01:21,137 --> 00:01:23,885
at the top right, so they are equal as

28
00:01:23,885 --> 00:01:25,771
well. In the same way, angle three equals angle

29
00:01:25,771 --> 00:01:28,508
seven, and angle four equals angle eight.

30
00:01:29,127 --> 00:01:32,540
Now look between the parallel lines. Angles four and

31
00:01:32,540 --> 00:01:36,312
five are on opposite sides of the transversal, so

32
00:01:36,312 --> 00:01:40,217
they are alternate interior angles, and they are equal.

33
00:01:40,217 --> 00:01:42,762
Angles three and six are the other alternate interior

34
00:01:42,762 --> 00:01:46,836
pair, and they are equal too. Alternate interior angles

35
00:01:46,836 --> 00:01:49,598
are always equal when the lines are parallel.

36
00:01:50,230 --> 00:01:54,307
One pair of interior angles behaves differently. Angles three

37
00:01:54,307 --> 00:01:55,890
and five are on the same side of the

38
00:01:55,890 --> 00:02:00,960
transversal, between the parallel lines. Because the lines are

39
00:02:00,960 --> 00:02:03,397
parallel, these same-side interior angles add up to one

40
00:02:03,397 --> 00:02:06,313
hundred and eighty degrees. Angles four and six are

41
00:02:06,313 --> 00:02:08,757
the other such pair, and they also add up

42
00:02:08,757 --> 00:02:10,681
to one hundred and eighty degrees.

43
00:02:11,313 --> 00:02:14,855
The exterior angles have their own two rules. Angles

44
00:02:14,855 --> 00:02:17,393
two and seven are on opposite sides of the

45
00:02:17,393 --> 00:02:22,553
transversal, outside the parallel lines: they are alternate exterior

46
00:02:22,553 --> 00:02:25,501
angles, and they are equal. Angles one and eight

47
00:02:25,501 --> 00:02:30,182
are the other alternate exterior pair, and they are

48
00:02:30,182 --> 00:02:32,576
equal too. Angles one and seven are on the

49
00:02:32,576 --> 00:02:35,665
same side, so they are same-side exterior angles, and

50
00:02:35,665 --> 00:02:38,430
they add up to one hundred and eighty degrees.

51
00:02:38,430 --> 00:02:40,693
Angles two and eight do the same, so both

52
00:02:40,693 --> 00:02:42,284
exterior rules are now in place.

53
00:02:42,730 --> 00:02:45,277
This is why the rules matter: every one of

54
00:02:45,277 --> 00:02:48,750
them turns a diagram into an equation. Step one:

55
00:02:48,750 --> 00:02:52,078
identify the pair. Angles three and five are same-side

56
00:02:52,078 --> 00:02:54,581
interior angles, so they add up to one hundred

57
00:02:54,581 --> 00:02:58,430
and eighty degrees. Step two: read the measures off

58
00:02:58,430 --> 00:03:01,404
the diagram: three x plus twenty, and five x

59
00:03:01,404 --> 00:03:05,650
minus eight. Step three: form the equation. Eight x

60
00:03:05,650 --> 00:03:08,181
plus twelve equals one hundred and eighty, so eight

61
00:03:08,181 --> 00:03:11,070
x is one hundred and sixty-eight. Step four: solve,

62
00:03:11,070 --> 00:03:15,897
and x is twenty-one. Step five: interpret. The angles

63
00:03:15,897 --> 00:03:18,540
are eighty-three degrees and ninety-seven degrees, and they do

64
00:03:18,540 --> 00:03:20,221
add up to one hundred and eighty.

65
00:03:20,843 --> 00:03:23,094
Let us use a second pair. These two angles

66
00:03:23,094 --> 00:03:25,377
are in the same position at the two crossings,

67
00:03:25,377 --> 00:03:28,782
so they are corresponding angles, and corresponding angles are

68
00:03:28,782 --> 00:03:31,067
equal. The diagram gives them as five x, and

69
00:03:31,067 --> 00:03:34,393
two x plus twenty-four. Equal angles give an equation:

70
00:03:34,393 --> 00:03:38,923
five x equals two x plus twenty-four. Subtracting two

71
00:03:38,923 --> 00:03:41,033
x from both sides leaves three x equals twenty-four.

72
00:03:41,033 --> 00:03:44,446
So x is eight. Both angles are forty degrees,

73
00:03:44,446 --> 00:03:48,154
which is exactly what equal angles should be.

74
00:03:48,637 --> 00:03:52,189
Your turn. Four quick checks. First: this pair sit

75
00:03:52,189 --> 00:03:54,777
in the same position at the two crossings. Are

76
00:03:54,777 --> 00:03:56,670
they equal, or do they add up to one

77
00:03:56,670 --> 00:03:59,975
hundred and eighty? Second: this pair lie between the

78
00:03:59,975 --> 00:04:04,547
parallel lines, on opposite sides of the transversal. Third:

79
00:04:04,547 --> 00:04:06,917
this pair lie between the lines, on the same

80
00:04:06,917 --> 00:04:09,455
side. And last of all: two corresponding angles are

81
00:04:09,455 --> 00:04:12,768
two x plus ten and three x minus thirty. Find x.

82
00:04:23,727 --> 00:04:25,836
The first pair are corresponding angles, so they are

83
00:04:25,836 --> 00:04:29,797
equal. The second pair are alternate interior angles, so

84
00:04:29,797 --> 00:04:32,284
they are equal as well. The third pair are

85
00:04:32,284 --> 00:04:35,219
same-side interior angles, so they add up to one

86
00:04:35,219 --> 00:04:39,507
hundred and eighty degrees. And for the last one:

87
00:04:39,507 --> 00:04:41,964
two x plus ten equals three x minus thirty,

88
00:04:41,964 --> 00:04:44,458
so x is forty, and each angle is ninety degrees.

89
00:04:45,097 --> 00:04:48,382
One last look at all six relationships. Corresponding angles

90
00:04:48,382 --> 00:04:51,762
are equal, alternate interior angles are equal, and so

91
00:04:51,762 --> 00:04:56,837
are alternate exterior angles. Vertically opposite angles are equal

92
00:04:56,837 --> 00:05:00,150
too. Same-side interior angles add up to one hundred

93
00:05:00,150 --> 00:05:03,854
and eighty degrees, and same-side exterior angles do the

94
00:05:03,854 --> 00:05:07,430
same. Geometry gives the rule, and the equation finds

95
00:05:07,430 --> 00:05:09,606
x. Thank you for watching, and see you in

96
00:05:09,606 --> 00:05:10,708
the next lesson.
